## ScummVM DGDS Behavioral Reference

This project regularly consults the [ScummVM DGDS engine](https://github.com/scummvm/scummvm/tree/master/engines/dgds)
to identify opcodes and cross-check parser, ADS scheduler, TTM run-flag, timing,
and composition behavior. In particular, the following upstream files are
important references:

- [`ads.cpp`](https://github.com/scummvm/scummvm/blob/master/engines/dgds/ads.cpp) — ADS conditions, active-segment evaluation, sequence run flags, and ordering operations;
- [`ttm.cpp`](https://github.com/scummvm/scummvm/blob/master/engines/dgds/ttm.cpp) — TTM parsing/execution, frame progression, drawing operations, and sequence reset behavior;
- [`ttm.h`](https://github.com/scummvm/scummvm/blob/master/engines/dgds/ttm.h) — TTM environment, sequence state, and run-type definitions.

ScummVM is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
later; its copyright remains with the ScummVM contributors. This repository
does not vendor those ScummVM source files. Bottle's JavaScript implementation
is maintained separately, with behavioral findings captured in local tests and
documentation. Contributions that copy or adapt upstream code must identify
that provenance and preserve all applicable license and copyright obligations.

