## CRT-Lottes Research Reference

The game and presentation lab share Timothy Lottes' **CRT-Lottes**
shader, whose preserved source header declares it public domain. The file is
unchanged from Libretro `glsl-shaders` revision
`e808ca09c699db7a843154cf7dc4dfd766d18a8a`:
https://github.com/libretro/glsl-shaders/blob/e808ca09c699db7a843154cf7dc4dfd766d18a8a/crt/shaders/crt-lottes.glsl

See `src/games/johnny/ui/crt/vendor/README.md` for provenance and the browser
adapter. The experimental VGA beam shader is original code. Creative, VGA beam and CRT-Lottes are selectable optional game models.


## Guest Advanced HD Research Pipeline

The development lab contains an experimental WebGL2 port of guest(r)'s
GPL-2.0-or-later Guest Advanced HD pipeline, pinned to Libretro revision
`77c52ce6b557bcb81ca298ae01ea955dd2792ba7`. Original headers, preset and shader
sources are preserved under `tools/presentation-lab/vendor/guest-hd/`, with full
license text in `COPYING` and corresponding browser adapter/source in the lab.
The Guest adapter and combined Guest demo are GPL-2.0-or-later; original MIT
components retain their compatible MIT terms. See the Guest README for scope,
source/build instructions and validation limits. Optional image LUTs are not
redistributed pending provenance. The production game does not import Guest.
